 "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step5-opus-aa-1017-omp36-aa/omp-36/cells/aa-1/trig-omp-reported/15/workspace", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "aa-2", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/17.3.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/5347ff91e8f44f2c69a79d7b152b7301687cd5c8/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`. It used `datetime.strptime` with a fixed format (`%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S`), which has no slot for a timezone, so the trailing `Z` caused the error. It now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)`, which understands `Z` on Python 3.11 and later; this environment runs 3.13.5. All 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` pass, including `test_naive` and `test_day_key`.\n\nBehaviour changes to be aware of:\n- **Timezone-aware results:** timestamps ending in `Z` now come back as UTC-aware datetimes. Comparing one with a naive datetime, or subtracting one from the other, raises `TypeError`. Timestamps without a suffix stay naive, as before.\n- **Wider input:** it now also accepts other ISO forms the old format rejected, such as offsets like `+02:00`, fractional seconds, and date-only strings.\n- **Python version:** the code now needs Python 3.11 or later. The repo has no version constraint, so I didn't add a fallback for older versions.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttl